nodecode-prompt-studio is a rewrite of bwoliveira's bwoliveira/prompt-studio:

  https://github.com/bwoliveira/prompt-studio
  commit ecead76f0b2ff4f46c09341c871e234eb1692a1a
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Bruno Oliveira (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the wizard and the three engines. The steps, their order and their
recommended answers come from the Desktop half (desktop/src/studio-core.js,
studio-state.js and ui-steps.js); the prompt itself comes from the per-model
engines (desktop/src/engine-opus.js, engine-sonnet.js, engine-astra.js): the
section order, the lines each guide asks for, the pasted-text handling with
its stable id and its escaping, the design-pattern defaults, the deliverable
lines, the done-when lines and the subagent rules. The answer parser and the
step report are new, because the sheet a person clicked is a line of text
here, and the polish replaces the per-step suggestion calls with one side call
on the auxiliary model, keeping the built prompt when a section comes back
missing.

Left out: the Desktop chrome, which a cell cannot draw -- the sheet, the
option cards with a key on every control, the F4 keybinding, the command
palette entry, the sparkle beside Send, the composer write-back and the
Send now button; the per-step suggestion pipeline (its prompts, its retry and
its per-request deadlines); the interface language switch; the installer and
its config writes; and the session-brief reader, since the tool's caller is
the model that already has the session. The plugin's own packaging -- plugin.yaml,
dashboard/, install.sh, the reproducibility and docs checks -- is Hermes's
rather than the plugin's behaviour.
